[center][size=5][b][color=#ffd966]Crafting Queue[/color][/b][/size]
[size=3]See what you need, what you have, and which chest it's in.[/size][/center]

Ever walk up to the workbench and forget what the recipe needed, or which chest the planks were in? Crafting Queue keeps a small to-do list on screen: [b]Ctrl + right-click[/b] anything to add it, and the panel shows what you have, what's missing and where it is.

[center][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/VERTO13/GK2-CraftingQueue/main/docs/images/usage.gif[/img][/center]

[size=4][b][color=#ffd966]Features[/color][/b][/size]

[b]Add from almost anywhere[/b]
[list]
[*]Ctrl + right-click works on items, station recipes, buildings, town works, quest requirements, NPC requests, vendor orders and tech tree blueprints.
[*]If the panel is folded because a window is open, it unfolds for a moment so you can see the new task.
[/list]
[center][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/VERTO13/GK2-CraftingQueue/main/docs/images/remove-and-blueprints.gif[/img][/center]

[b]The recipe tree, only for what's missing[/b]
[list]
[*]A task asks to [i]have[/i] that many: what you already own counts, and the recipe below covers only what's still missing.
[*]If something can be made at more than one station, or with more than one recipe, flip between them with ◂ ▸. Each option shows its own station, yield and ingredients.
[*]Real yields: the ×N includes your perks and talents, including a zombie's if one works that station.
[*]Only what you can actually use: locked recipes and stations stay hidden, and show up on their own once you unlock them.
[/list]
[center][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/VERTO13/GK2-CraftingQueue/main/docs/images/multi-recipe.gif[/img][/center]

[b]See which chest has it[/b]
[list]
[*]Little bubbles over the chests and storages in your zone show which of your materials each one holds.
[*]Hover a task in the panel to preview where its materials are, or pin it to keep them marked.
[*]Short here? The row tells you where else you have it, in grey: "· Yard: 7".
[/list]
[center][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/VERTO13/GK2-CraftingQueue/main/docs/images/chest-bubbles.png[/img][/center]

[b]Peek at any recipe[/b]
[list]
[*]Hold [b]Alt[/b] over any item, in your inventory, a chest or the panel itself, to see its full recipe without adding it.
[/list]
[center][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/VERTO13/GK2-CraftingQueue/main/docs/images/alt-view.gif[/img][/center]

[b]And also[/b]
[list]
[*]Tasks that share a material split it in queue order. Reorder them with ▲ ▼ to set priorities.
[*]Tasks leave the list on their own once you craft, pick up or buy what was missing.
[*]Stays out of the way: with a chest, station or the tech tree open, the panel moves aside or folds into a small tab. The eye icon keeps it always visible.
[*]Pixel-crisp at 720p, 1080p, 1440p and 4K. Very light (about 0.1 ms per frame).
[*]One queue per save slot. 16 languages, following the game's language.
[/list]

[size=4][b][color=#ffd966]Controls[/color][/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Ctrl + right-click[/b] – add to the queue
[*][b]Alt[/b] (hold) – show a recipe
[*][b]F3[/b] – show / hide the panel
[*][b]F4[/b] – detailed / compact recipes
[*]Hover a task – its ▲ ▼ − + and trash buttons, and its pin
[*]Gamepad [i](experimental)[/i]: tap [b]R3[/b] on a slot to add it, hold R3 to see its recipe, R3 in the world to use the panel
[/list]

[size=4][b][color=#ffd966]Installation[/color][/b][/size]
[list=1]
[*]Close the game.
[*]In Steam, right-click [b]Graveyard Keeper 2[/b] → [b]Manage[/b] → [b]Browse local files[/b]. That's your game folder.
[*]Extract the zip into that folder (choose [b]Replace[/b] if asked). You should see a [b]BepInEx[/b] folder next to [b]GraveyardKeeper2.exe[/b].
[*]Start the game and load your save: the [b]Queue[/b] panel appears at the top right.
[/list]
Pick [b]"with BepInEx"[/b] if this is your first BepInEx mod, or the [b]mod-only[/b] file if you already have BepInEx 5 or are updating. Your queue is kept when you update.

[b]Uninstall:[/b] delete [code]BepInEx\plugins\CraftingQueue[/code] in your game folder.

[size=4][b][color=#ffd966]Good to know[/color][/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Requires [url=https://github.com/BepInEx/BepInEx/releases/tag/v5.4.23.5]BepInEx 5.4.23.x[/url] (included in the "with BepInEx" file).
[*]No balance or gameplay changes, and your save is never touched: the queue lives in its own file per save slot.
[*]While you hold Ctrl, right-click adds to the queue instead of doing its normal action.
[*]No network access, no data collection, no game files or assets included.
[*]Works alongside other mods.
[*]Still in beta, so expect a few bugs. Gamepad support is experimental.
[/list]

[size=4][b][color=#ffd966]Bugs and source code[/color][/b][/size]
Found a bug? Please report it in the [b]Bugs[/b] tab or on [url=https://github.com/VERTO13/GK2-CraftingQueue/issues/new/choose]GitHub[/url], with a screenshot and the file [code]BepInEx\LogOutput.log[/code] from your game folder.

Open source (MIT): [url=https://github.com/VERTO13/GK2-CraftingQueue]github.com/VERTO13/GK2-CraftingQueue[/url]
